[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Read by tenant, form and body, its
reports show two causes, and five reports that fit neither. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October:
the parser is fixed, the hint is won't fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The parser fix (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`) covers the parser reports.
The hint is won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {issues} {moveIssue} />

## The problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first, so a date like 4/7 becomes 7 April instead of 4 July. Most of #4471 is this.

**`hint`: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** People at day-first
tenants type month first, as told, and the form reads the date the tenant's way. This happens
only through the form, and only at booking-v3 tenants. Fixing the parser does not fix it: the hint
is wrong.

**`one-day move`: the date moves by one day, not swapped.** The desk noted these in
`desk-notes.json` and then filed them under the parser by tenant. They say "one day off", "the
invite arrived before I made the booking", and "Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday". A month
and day swap cannot do that. It looks like a timezone conversion.

## How they were counted

- Reports are unique by id. The ticket export repeats some reports across overlapping pages.
- The cause comes from the tenant (`causes.ts`): its locale and its booking form. `intakeTag` is
  intake's guess from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the tenant in both directions.
- The reports in `desk-notes.json` stay counted under the cause their tenant puts them in, as
  the desk counts them, and are footnoted there.

## Tickets

- [#1](https://github.com/erik-farmer/mega-s01e03/issues/1) `parser`: closed, completed: fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- [#2](https://github.com/erik-farmer/mega-s01e03/issues/2) `hint`: closed, not planned: won't fix, the booking-v3 form is retired.
- [#3](https://github.com/erik-farmer/mega-s01e03/issues/3) `one-day move`: closed as a duplicate of #1, where the desk counts these reports.

## Lessons

- A matching subject line does not mean the same cause. Read the tenant, the channel and the body.
- A note that says "read differently" is a finding. Give it its own ticket.

